{
  "summary": "This study investigates closed nanopores in silicon-carbon anodes as stress-regulation units to mitigate lithiation-induced deformation and interphase degradation. By engineering heteroatom-doped carbon hosts with abundant closed pores, the material redirects expansion stress internally, reducing electrode swelling. The nitrogen-doped composite achieves 1756.5 mAh g-1 reversible capacity, 90.2% initial Coulombic efficiency, and 868.4 mAh g-1 at 3 C, with 13.1% thickness expansion after 50 cycles. The approach demonstrates scalable production and enhanced cycling stability for practical lithium-ion batteries.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Closed nanopores in heteroatom-doped carbon hosts redirect lithiation-induced stress internally, reducing electrode swelling",
    "Nitrogen-doped silicon-carbon composite achieves 1756.5 mAh g-1 reversible capacity and 90.2% initial Coulombic efficiency",
    "The material reduces thickness expansion from 38.4% to 13.1% after 50 cycles and enables 80% capacity retention in 1200 cycles for NCM811 pouch cells"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes closed-pore stress regulation as a scalable structural strategy for practical low-expansion silicon-carbon anodes, advancing battery electrode design for high-energy applications."
}

{
  "summary": "This study integrated single-cell epigenomic data from 2.5 million adult mouse brain nuclei to construct a comprehensive atlas. It combined histone modifications, transcriptomes, chromatin accessibility, DNA methylation, and 3D genome organization to define 100+ cell subclasses and chromatin states across 81% of the genome. Active states with combinatorial histone marks better identify functional enhancers than accessibility alone, while H3K27me3 and H3K9me3 define repressive states. The atlas enables deep learning models for predicting epigenomic features and gene expression from DNA sequence.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Integration of four histone modifications, transcriptomes, chromatin accessibility, DNA methylation, and 3D genome data across 2.5 million nuclei",
    "Active chromatin states defined by combinatorial histone modifications better identify functional enhancers than chromatin accessibility alone",
    "H3K27me3- and H3K9me3-marked chromatin states delineate distinct modes of cell-type-specific gene repression"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This atlas provides a unified framework for annotating the regulatory genome of the adult mouse brain and interpreting non-coding disease risk variants through multi-modal epigenomic integration."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates enhancing the biodegradation of compostable polyesters in deep-sea environments by embedding enzymes within them. The researchers tested enzyme-embedded polyesters (PBS, PBSA, PCL, PBAT) at depths up to 5,503 meters. Results showed near-complete degradation at 757 meters within five months and moderate degradation at extreme depths. The approach maintains mechanical properties while enabling rapid marine breakdown.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Enzyme-embedded polyesters degraded near-completely at 757 m deep-sea depth within five months",
    "Moderate biodegradation occurred at extreme depths of 5,503 m",
    "Mechanical properties remained comparable to enzyme-free polyesters"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This strategy provides a scalable method for accelerating marine biodegradation of compostable plastics, addressing a critical gap in deep-sea plastic pollution mitigation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigated how protein kinase A (PKA) signaling regulates group 3 innate lymphoid cell (ILC3) homeostasis and its role in gut inflammation. Using a single-cell atlas, researchers found that prostaglandin activates PKA to promote tissue-protective functions, while interleukin-23 (IL-23) suppresses PKA inhibitors. Deletion of PRKAR1A reduced ILC3s and increased infection susceptibility in mice. IL-23 overproduction decreased PRKAR1A, increasing PKA signaling and gut inflammation. Human ILC3s express PRKAR1A, which is downregulated by IL-23 or in inflammatory bowel disease.",
  "key_findings": [
    "ILC3s maintain tissue-protective functions via PKA signaling regulated by prostaglandin",
    "IL-23 suppresses PKA inhibitors, reducing ILC3 numbers and increasing infection susceptibility",
    "IL-23 overproduction decreases PRKAR1A, increasing PKA signaling and gut inflammation in mice"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes PKA signaling as a critical regulator of ILC3 homeostasis, revealing how IL-23-driven PKA dysregulation contributes to gut inflammation."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates the emergence of a Chern metal in frustrated moiré Kondo lattices. Using angle-aligned MoTe2/WSe2 bilayers, researchers observed a compressible state with nearly quantized Hall resistance and finite longitudinal resistance. Nonlocal transport confirmed chiral edge states, while magnetic circular dichroism revealed a magnetization plateau preceding a metamagnetic transition at Kondo breakdown. The findings demonstrate how moiré engineering can stabilize topological quantum phases through Kondo interactions.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Observation of a compressible Chern metal state with nearly quantized Hall resistance",
    "Nonlocal transport measurements confirmed chiral edge states",
    "Magnetic circular dichroism showed a magnetization plateau before Kondo breakdown"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes moiré engineering as a pathway to stabilize topological quantum phases by coupling band topology with Kondo interactions."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates kinetic-environmental coupling at the buried interface in ambient flexible perovskite solar cells. Using dual-side in situ photoluminescence, researchers discovered simultaneous nucleation at gas-liquid and liquid-solid interfaces during antisolvent processing. Outward solvent evaporation delays α-phase conversion at the buried interface, exacerbating moisture attack. The authors designed a self-segregating molecule (NFA) that enriches at the buried interface to synchronize crystallization, passivate defects, and form a hydrophobic barrier. This approach achieved record power-conversion efficiencies of 24.84% (0.09 cm²) and 21.46% on mini-modules, maintaining 96.26% efficiency after 1000 h damp aging at 85 ± 5% RH.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Simultaneous nucleation occurs at both gas-liquid and liquid-solid interfaces during antisolvent processing",
    "Outward solvent evaporation delays α-phase conversion at the buried interface, exacerbating moisture attack",
    "Self-segregating molecule NFA synchronizes crystallization, passivates defects, and forms a hydrophobic barrier"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes self-segregated interfacial regulation as a rational strategy to overcome kinetic-environmental constraints in scalable flexible perovskite solar cells."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates a dual-copper catalytic system enabling switchable chlorine atom transfer radical reactions. The approach uses a dinuclear copper complex to activate unactivated alkyl chlorides and a mononuclear copper catalyst for controlled C-Cl bond reconstruction. The reaction switches between atom transfer radical addition (ATRA) and atom transfer radical polymerization (ATRP) depending on the presence of the mononuclear copper partner. The protocol facilitates synthesis of diverse ATRA products and α-end-functionalized polyacrylates, and allows direct modification of poly(vinyl chloride) under mild conditions.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A dinuclear copper complex selectively activates robust C-Cl bonds in unactivated alkyl chlorides",
    "A mononuclear copper catalyst mediates controlled C-Cl bond reconstruction for reaction switching",
    "The system enables synthesis of structurally diverse ATRA products and direct PVC modification under mild conditions"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes a versatile platform for chlorine atom transfer radical reactions using unactivated alkyl chlorides, advancing synthetic strategies for functionalized small molecules and polymers."
}

{
  "summary": "This study generated a whole-vertebrate single-cell transcriptome atlas using region-stratified single-cell RNA sequencing and spatial transcriptomics in the transparent teleost Danion as a model. It identified spatially distinct neural cell types, adult molecular positional memory, paedomorphic features, and conserved body-region specification programs. The atlas provides a resource for understanding vertebrate cell type composition, organization, and evolutionary mechanisms.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Identification of spatially distinct neural cell types based on regional gene expression signatures",
    "Discovery of adult molecular positional memory in specific cell types",
    "Uncovering paedomorphic features and conserved body-region and appendage-specification programs in adult connective tissue"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This whole-vertebrate single-cell atlas advances understanding of vertebrate cell type composition, spatial organization, and evolutionary conservation across species."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates amorphization of organic small molecule 2,3,7,8-tetraamino-5,10-dihydrophenazine-1,4,6,9-tetraone (TDT) to enhance active site exposure in aqueous ammonium-ion batteries. By disrupting π-π stacking, the amorphous TDT achieves high surface area (738 m² g⁻¹), delivers 242.8 mAh g⁻¹ at 0.1 A g⁻¹, and maintains 87.1% capacity after 817 cycles. In situ measurements confirm NH₄⁺ adsorption via coordination/deprotonation and hydrolysis-driven proton storage, enabling a 100,000-cycle full cell and practical Ah-level pouch cell performance.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Amorphous TDT disrupts π-π stacking to expose buried redox sites",
    "Amorphous TDT achieves 242.8 mAh g⁻¹ capacity at 0.1 A g⁻¹ with 87.1% retention after 817 cycles",
    "In situ evidence shows NH₄⁺ adsorption via coordination/deprotonation and hydrolysis-driven proton storage"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work demonstrates that amorphization of organic small molecules can unlock active sites for high-capacity, long-cycle aqueous ammonium-ion batteries, advancing sustainable energy storage solutions."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines molecular mechanisms driving inflammatory rheumatic diseases including rheumatoid arthritis, psoriatic arthritis, and systemic lupus eryusing dysregulated innate and adaptive immunity. It evaluates recent advances in understanding disease pathogenesis and identifies emerging therapeutic targets that could enable more effective disease control and potential cures for these previously chronic conditions.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Dysregulation of innate and adaptive immune responses underlies inflammatory rheumatic diseases",
    "Recent advances reveal molecular mechanisms contributing to disease pathogenesis",
    "Emerging therapeutic targets offer potential for improved disease control and cures"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This study advances understanding of immune dysregulation in rheumatic diseases and provides a foundation for developing targeted therapies that may transform chronic inflammatory conditions into manageable or curable disorders."
}

{
  "summary": "This study quantified genetic diversity loss in 62 songbird species from China's Gaol. Mountains biodiversity hotspot by comparing historical and modern genomes. It found genomic erosion averaging 43-49%, disproportionately affecting common species. The loss is driven by habitat fragmentation, exceeds conservation thresholds, and persists despite species being listed as 'Least Concern' on the IUCN Red List, highlighting a critical gap in extinction risk monitoring.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Genomic erosion averaged 43-49% across 62 songbird species in a Chinese biodiversity hotspot",
    "Common species were disproportionately affected by genetic diversity loss",
    "The erosion exceeds conservation policy thresholds and persists despite IUCN 'Least Concern' listings"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study demonstrates that genetic diversity loss in songbirds can occur rapidly in biodiversity hotspots, challenging current conservation metrics and underscoring the need for genomic assessments in extinction risk monitoring."
}

{
  "summary": "This review establishes a state-centered framework for organic mixed ionic-electronic conductors (OMIECs), moving beyond scalar descriptors like voltage or charge. It introduces a minimal sufficient state basis to distinguish essential coordinates, while waveform history and spatial heterogeneity determine when lumped descriptions are valid. The framework enables reconstructing hidden states and designing multidimensional electrochemical trajectories for applications such as electrochromics, OECTs, and energy storage devices.",
  "key_findings": [
    "A minimal sufficient state basis identifies essential coordinates for OMIECs",
    "Waveform history and spatial heterogeneity define validity of lumped state descriptions",
    "The framework enables reconstruction of hidden states and trajectory design for electrochemical applications"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This framework provides a unified approach to model and design electrochemical states in OMIECs, advancing understanding of how molecular structure, device architecture, and driving protocols influence observable, reversible, and durable electrochemical trajectories."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates factors influencing early human settlement in arid regions, focusing on the role of stone availability alongside water. Using a 1,500-km geoarchaeological survey across the Rub' al Khali desert, researchers found no lithic artefacts or knappable materials despite abundant freshwater at 55 of 125 sites. Spatial modeling indicates settlement required co-occurrence of water and stone resources, with 57% of water-accessible terrain lacking suitable stone. The findings suggest raw-material geology constrains human dispersal beyond water availability alone.",
  "key_findings": [
    "No lithic artefacts or knappable raw materials were found along a 1,500-km transect despite abundant freshwater",
    "57% of water-accessible terrain lacks knappable stone, indicating stone availability as a critical constraint",
    "Spatial modeling shows settlement tracked co-occurrence of water and lithic resources, not water alone"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study demonstrates that stone availability, not water, was a key constraint on early human dispersal into arid regions, challenging models that prioritize water availability alone."
}

{
  "summary": "This study compared global bird song corpora across vocal learners (oscines and hummingbirds) and nonlearners (suboscines, nightjars) with human speech and song data. It found recurring acoustic patterns between bird songs and human vocalizations, with resemblance varying between speech and song. Vocal learning did not alter acoustic patterning or similarity to human vocalizations, indicating deep evolutionary analogies in vocal communication mechanisms.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Recurring acoustic patterns exist between bird songs and human speech/song across multiple vocal learner and nonlearner groups",
    "Resemblance between bird songs and human vocalizations varies depending on whether it relates to speech or song",
    "Vocal learning does not systematically affect acoustic patterning or similarity to human vocalizations"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study reveals deep evolutionary parallels in vocal communication mechanisms between birds and humans, highlighting convergent acoustic patterning despite divergent evolutionary paths."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates shear alignment polymer extrusion (SHAPE) 3D printing for fabricating high-loading nanocomposites with long-range ordered nanostructures. The approach uses high shear forces to align nanofillers like boron nitride nanosheets and carbon nanotubes in polymer matrices, enabling scalable production of complex 3D architectures. Results demonstrate 55 wt% boron nitride in polylactic acid filaments with zero volume shrinkage post-sintering, exceptional thermomechanical stability, and tailored thermal conductivity (1.07 W/m/K) and mechanical properties.",
  "key_findings": [
    "SHAPE 3D printing achieves 55 wt% boron nitride nanosheets in polylactic acid filaments",
    "Post-sintering nanocomposites exhibit zero volume shrinkage and thermomechanical stability up to polymer decomposition temperatures",
    "Vertically aligned BN composites show enhanced thermal conductivity (1.07 W/m/K) while horizontally aligned structures provide thermal insulation (0.071 W/m/K)"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This method enables scalable fabrication of high-loading nanocomposites with long-range ordered nanostructures, advancing cross-scale design for thermal management and structural applications."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates Clostridium perfringens Delta toxin's role in necrotizing enterocolitis (NEC) and associated brain injury. Researchers identified Delta toxin-positive C. perfringens in severe NEC cases, demonstrating its ability to induce intestinal necrosis and cerebral injury via macrophage targeting. The toxin binds host receptor CD9, triggering inflammation and blood-brain barrier disruption. Therapeutic neutralization of Delta toxin showed protective effects.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Delta toxin-positive C. perfringens is present in severe NEC cases and causes intestinal necrosis and brain injury",
    "Delta toxin targets CD9 on macrophages, activating inflammasomes and pyroptosis to disrupt the blood-brain barrier",
    "Neutralizing anti-Delta toxin antibodies protect against disease progression"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work identifies a specific microbial toxin pathway driving a subset of NEC and brain injury, establishing Delta toxin-CD9 interaction as a target for precision therapy."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates whether the brain functions as a host defense effector in immune responses. Using a model of systemic immune activation, researchers assessed brain immune activity. Findings indicate the brain exhibits immune effector mechanisms during systemic immune challenges, suggesting it may contribute to host defense beyond traditional peripheral sites.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The brain demonstrates immune effector activity during systemic immune activation",
    "Brain immune responses correlate with systemic immune challenges",
    "The brain may serve as an additional host defense site beyond conventional peripheral immune organs"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes the brain as a potential active participant in systemic host defense, expanding understanding of immune system organization beyond peripheral tissues."
}

{
  "summary": "This study addresses the long-standing challenge of achieving stable photocatalytic pure water splitting over Ta3N5 by identifying incompatibility between cocatalysts in alkaline systems and pure water splitting as a critical bottleneck. A highly dispersed RuCoOx cocatalyst was developed using a multi-step incipient wetness impregnation strategy. The optimized Pt@Cr2O3/Ta3N5/RuCoOx system achieved stoichiometric water splitting with an apparent quantum yield of 0.72% at 420 nm, the highest for Ta-based nitrides to date. The findings indicate enhanced interfacial electric fields and reduced reaction barriers improve hole extraction and intermediate kinetics.",
  "key_findings": [
    "The optimized Pt@Cr2O3/Ta3N5/RuCoOx system achieved stoichiometric water splitting with 0.72% apparent quantum yield at 420 nm",
    "Enhanced interfacial electric fields facilitated hole extraction, improving charge separation",
    "Reduced formation barriers for key intermediates accelerated surface reaction kinetics"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work establishes cocatalyst compatibility as a critical design principle for stable photocatalytic water splitting in nitride-based materials, advancing mechanistic understanding of charge dynamics in pure water splitting systems."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates monolithic in situ integration of lead sulfide (PbS) infrared detectors directly onto readout integrated circuits (ROICs) using a room-temperature aqueous process. By controlling Pb-OH complexation and minimizing environmental interference, the researchers achieved quasi-single-crystalline PbS films with high electronic properties and pixel-level uniformity. The fabricated 640×512-pixel array demonstrated record-specific detectivity at 2.5 µm, enabling clear infrared imaging and flexible ROIC integration.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Quasi-single-crystalline PbS films with carrier density ~2×10^15 cm^-3 and mobility 124 cm^2 V^-1 s^-1",
    "Record specific detectivity of 4.4×10^11 Jones at 2.5 µm, exceeding commercial InGaAs detectors",
    "640×512-pixel focal-plane array capturing clear infrared images and direct integration onto flexible ROICs"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This solution-based monolithic integration method provides a scalable pathway for high-performance infrared detectors, advancing optoelectronic sensor technology without traditional bonding processes."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates how rapid east-west migration affects the Sun compass in Manx shearwaters. Using GPS tracking, researchers found that long-distance homing flights cause time shifts, leading to predictable errors in Sun compass orientation despite access to alternative navigation cues. The results highlight the interplay between endogenous clocks and celestial navigation in migratory species.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Rapid longitudinal flights induce time shifts in Manx shear:ers",
    "Sun compass errors persist even with compass-independent cues during coast following",
    "Endogenous clocks and celestial navigation interact during long-distance migration"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "The study demonstrates that rapid east-west movement disrupts endogenous circadian timing, providing critical insights into how chronobiological mechanisms constrain navigational accuracy across migratory pathways."
}

{
  "summary": "This study quantifies magnetic interactions in Fe3GeTe2/graphite/Fe3GeTe2 heterostructures using cross-sectional Lorentz transmission electron microscopy and off-axis electron holography. It reconstructs local projected magnetic induction within and between layers, revealing domain alignment weakens with increasing separation. The stray-field coupling length scale is λ=37±7 nm, corresponding to a 23% reduction in interlayer magnetic induction relative to bulk FGT. This near-surface effect guides device design for controllable magnetic coupling.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Stray-field coupling length scale of λ=37±7 nm for FGT/FGT heterostructures",
    "23% reduction in interlayer magnetic induction relative to bulk FGT at λ",
    "Near-surface magnetic induction reduction up to ∼100 nm from surfaces"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides quantitative characterization of magnetic coupling in stacked van der Waals magnets, enabling precise engineering of magnetic interactions in heterostructure-based devices."
}

{
  "summary": "This study investigates spin injection from Mn5Si3, a compensated magnet with zero net magnetization. Using lateral spin-valve devices, researchers electrically injected spins into a non-magnetic channel and detected propagation at a ferromagnetic electrode. Time-reversed magnetic states of Mn5Si3 reversed the spin signal, indicating time-reversal-symmetry-breaking spin injection. The findings demonstrate that compensated magnets can generate spin currents controlled by magnetic order without net magnetization, with spin polarizations of 6.5-10% and diffusion lengths of 50-130 nm.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Spin injection from Mn5Si3, a compensated magnet with vanishing net magnetization, breaks time-reversal symmetry",
    "Time-reversed magnetic states of Mn5Si3 reverse the detected spin signal",
    "Spin polarizations of 6.5-10% and diffusion lengths of 50-130 nm are observed"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work provides experimental evidence that compensated magnets can generate spin currents via altermagnetic order, enabling spintronic functionality without net magnetization."
}

{
  "summary": "This study provides a weekly compilation of newly introduced scientific instrumentation, apparatus, and laboratory materials potentially relevant to research. The approach involves curating and summarizing recent product offerings from the scientific community. The main finding is the systematic listing of emerging tools and resources without specific performance metrics or comparative analysis. The results indicate a continuous flow of new laboratory resources available for researchers.",
  "key_findings": [
    "Weekly compilation of newly introduced scientific instrumentation and laboratory materials",
    "Focus on products of potential interest to researchers without performance metrics",
    "Systematic listing of emerging tools without comparative analysis"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This work contributes to the transparency of scientific resource availability by documenting new laboratory tools and materials as they become available to the research community."
}

{
  "summary": "This review examines aluminum scandium nitride (AlScN) as a next-generation semiconductor for ferroelectric and piezoelectric applications. It investigates physical mechanisms enabling enhanced ferroelectric switching and piezoelectric responses via scandium doping in aluminum nitride. The study identifies challenges in high-quality epitaxial film growth, including ferroelectric endurance limitations, interface instability, and leakage currents. Recent advances in AlScN applications for ferroelectric memories, radio-frequency circuits, and high-electron-mobility transistors are highlighted, emphasizing potential for energy-efficient computing and AI hardware.",
  "key_findings": [
    "AlScN exhibits improved ferroelectric switching and piezoelectric responses due to scandium doping in aluminum nitride",
    "High-quality AlScN epitaxial films face challenges such as reduced ferroelectric endurance and interface instability",
    "Recent progress enables AlScN applications in ferroelectric memories, radio-frequency circuits, and high-electron-mobility transistors"
  ],
  "scientific_significance": "This review establishes AlScN's potential to enable energy-efficient computing and AI hardware through optimized ferroelectric and piezoelectric mechanisms."
}
